                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92b3c043-7209-328b-9460-b08f2e805628",
                        "entry_id": "8279bafb-fe80-38e5-8d44-2fc5646cf4f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle qui cherche."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10308cc4-ab41-4144-8783-6067e44c13be",
                                "sense_id": "92b3c043-7209-328b-9460-b08f2e805628",
                                "text": "Les titres qui font recettes ? La chercheuse d’esprit de Charles Simon Favart, jouée deux cents fois de suite après sa création en 1741, ou encore Arlequin, roi de Serendib de Lesage, Les troqueurs de Vadé et Dauvergne en 1753…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e5b2f49-f693-35d3-9b1c-dd2e4722e082",
                        "entry_id": "8279bafb-fe80-38e5-8d44-2fc5646cf4f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Femme, qui seule ou membre d’une équipe, se consacre à la recherche scientifique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bf22be1-86af-42da-8e48-c76f855c74ed",
                                "sense_id": "3e5b2f49-f693-35d3-9b1c-dd2e4722e082",
                                "text": "La chercheuse a estimé, en dernier ressort, être la seule personne responsable de la validité des contenus. Ainsi, elle s’est réservée le jugement final quant à la pertinence de l’intégration des éléments d’analyse apportés par le groupe ou les intermédiaires. Tout en valorisant le savoir du groupe, la chercheuse, pendant le processus, a donc gardé la maîtrise de l’interprétation des résultats et des modalités de cette interprétation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bde89433-6922-42e2-962f-50ba4ac9ee64",
                                "sense_id": "3e5b2f49-f693-35d3-9b1c-dd2e4722e082",
                                "text": "L’épiderme du chef de l’État en danger ? Cette crainte est exprimée par deux très sérieuses docteures en pharmacie, chercheuses et enseignantes au laboratoire de pharmacie industrielle et de cosmétologie de la faculté de Nantes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38ed2266-3f49-49d7-8306-a5306c83353e",
                                "sense_id": "3e5b2f49-f693-35d3-9b1c-dd2e4722e082",
                                "text": "Il faut laisser le temps au spectateur de reprendre l’habitude de se rendre dans les salles, pondère Stéphanie Pourquier-Jacquin, chercheuse au Conservatoire national des arts et métiers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "be08ce27-446d-4897-af4a-ec5e6c35a6bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "8279bafb-fe80-38e5-8d44-2fc5646cf4f8",
                        "source_sense_description": "Femme qui cherche",
                        "target_lang_word": "searcher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "searcher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aca0c5f8-6475-3bdc-9bfd-4359a8a2ecb4",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who searches."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89ad04e0-f799-4548-bd2b-46ed44cbf491",
                                                "sense_id": "aca0c5f8-6475-3bdc-9bfd-4359a8a2ecb4",
                                                "text": "When he had repoſed four years and four months in the boſom of care, rocked in the cradle of proſperity, he was brought forth, according to the cuſtom of true believers, and committed to the charge of moralifts of high fame, poliſhers of noble manners, and ſearchers of true knowledge, that they might cultivate his heaven-born genius, and teach him with dignity to rule that world which he was born to command[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a00378f2-84b1-3aaa-8f8a-3fc774267b6c",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An officer in London appointed to examine the bodies of the dead, and report the cause of death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "027547b7-6873-4bbd-b4a0-aa4d20e56fb8",
                                                "sense_id": "a00378f2-84b1-3aaa-8f8a-3fc774267b6c",
                                                "text": "The Searchers hereupon (who are ancient Matrons, sworn to their Office) repair to the place where the dead Corps lies"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d983bd2-dddd-3192-8f99-1afa344d89f2",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An officer who apprehended idlers on the street during church hours in Scotland."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e565bb3d-37a2-3860-a6d4-48fa95992dfa",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A customs officer responsible for searching ships, merchandise, luggage, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37589d4a-5f3a-3389-bcc5-1a6dc94bba65",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inspector of leather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fb19ee2-b684-42b9-8993-e8b5832aae79",
                                                "sense_id": "37589d4a-5f3a-3389-bcc5-1a6dc94bba65",
                                                "text": "62. Leather Searcher and Sealer, functions of. The offices of Leather Searcher and Sealer are united in one person. He examines and seals all hides and leather, receiving some small fees of the parties for so doing, but has no salary or perquisites from the corporation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "250bc570-8000-4d97-8cc1-9a10f5f21287",
                                                "sense_id": "37589d4a-5f3a-3389-bcc5-1a6dc94bba65",
                                                "text": "Means adopted by tanners to evade the searcher's and sealer's inspection"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f27c79b-9a6e-40a9-b42c-9ec32822d1cf",
                                                "sense_id": "37589d4a-5f3a-3389-bcc5-1a6dc94bba65",
                                                "text": "THE OATH OF SEARCHERS AND SEALERS OF LETHER ^([sic]). You & eu'y of you shall well & truly view & search all & eu'y tanned hide skinne or Leather which shall be brought to any faire or m'kett within the p'cincts of the towne of Louth […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84927d8-9c36-4100-bd69-898d59fa8783",
                                                "sense_id": "37589d4a-5f3a-3389-bcc5-1a6dc94bba65",
                                                "text": "In 1362 William Drydale was the elected ale-taster, a manorial office like that of the leather searcher or pinder."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be959038-d903-332b-8d01-10048fcce30b",
                                        "entry_id": "c355aae3-7035-33e9-8c35-c6c4196d9774",
